**/node_modules
**/.cache
**/tmp
**/build
**/.git
# NOTE: tests/ is intentionally NOT excluded here. `server/php/Dockerfile`'s
# `test` stage runs `vendor/bin/phpunit` against `src/be/tests/` as the
# build-time quality gate, and `COPY src/be/ ./` (used by both `deps` and
# `deps-prod`) draws from this same build context — excluding tests/ here
# previously made PHPUnit fail with "Test directory tests/Unit not found"
# because the files never reached the image at all. Test files are instead
# explicitly removed from the `deps-prod` stage (which `runtime` is built
# from) via `RUN rm -rf tests phpunit.xml`, so they still never ship in the
# production image — see that stage's comment in the Dockerfile.
**/*.log
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.env
# Laravel's compiled bootstrap cache (packages.php, services.php, config.php,
# routes caches, ...) is host/environment-specific and regenerated on demand —
# never ship whatever happens to exist on the machine that ran `docker build`.
# `.gitignore` already keeps these files out of git; this keeps them out of
# the Docker build context too.
**/bootstrap/cache/*.php
# `vendor/` (no `**/` prefix, below) only matches a top-level ./vendor — it
# never matched the real path, `src/be/vendor/`, so a `vendor/` directory
# that happened to exist on the host (e.g. from a one-off local `composer
# install`, which should never happen under CLAUDE.md decision 2, but did)
# was silently copied into every stage by `COPY src/be/ ./`, clobbering the
# vendor/ that stage's own `composer install` had just produced. Concretely,
# this is what made `deps-prod`'s `composer install --no-dev` get overwritten
# by a full dev install copied in from the host, and the subsequent
# `composer dump-autoload --no-dev` then failed with "Class
# Laravel\Pail\PailServiceProvider not found" — a require-dev-only package's
# leftover discovery metadata colliding with a --no-dev autoload rebuild.
# `**/vendor` (anchored at any depth, matching the `**/node_modules`
# convention already used above) is the real fix; every stage must build its
# own vendor/ via `composer install`, never inherit one from the build host.
**/vendor
node_modules/
*.log
node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-debug.log
yarn-error.log

coverage

build
dist

.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
README.md